# To keep a folder's contents, use "!":
!README.md

# Don't include the data (downloaded genomes, annotations, and Illumina and Nanopore sequence data)
data/*

# To keep the READMEs, apparently I need to unignore and then reignore ALL subfolders and their contents  
!data/ncbi-genomes/
data/ncbi-genomes/*

!data/ncbi-annotated-cds/
data/ncbi-annotated-cds/*

!data/ncbi-annotated-proteins/
data/ncbi-annotated-proteins/*

!data/illumina-sequencing/
data/illumina-sequencing/*
!data/illumina-sequencing/raw-reads/
data/illumina-sequencing/raw-reads/*
!data/illumina-sequencing/trimmed-reads/
data/illumina-sequencing/trimmed-reads/*

!data/nanopore-sequencing/
data/nanopore-sequencing/*

# Blanket statement to keep all README.md files in order to preserve folder structure 
# **/ is needed for READMEs at any depth 
!**/README.md
 
